  "worked_solution": "We model the amount using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.072A.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nA(t)={A}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.072t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${A}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $320$ plants, so we have ${A}_{0}=320.$\n\nTherefore, the amount $A$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nA(t)=320\\,{e}^{0.072t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the amount when $t=9,$ we substitute $t=9$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(9) & =320\\,{e}^{0.072\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =320\\,{e}^{0.648} \\\\  & \u2248611.53\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the amount of the plant species after $9$ years is approximately $612$ plants.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
